COLOUR_LANGUAGE='Teal: cabin air; amber: differential-pressure load; blue: structural acrylic; grey: scratch protector; muted red: hypothetical failure.'
def sequences(at,S,dur):
    items=[('Passenger question',0,S('layers'),'An ordinary rounded window, seen through the scratch protector; push toward the hole.','Question and cruise setting'),('Reveal layers',S('layers'),S('pressure'),'The lit assembly rotates and separates into three real extruded panes. Physical leaders stay attached. Only the inner pane has a vent.','Scratch / Inner / Outer'),('Air enters gap',S('pressure'),at('pressure','normally'),'A teal path crosses the inner vent and terminates inside the structural gap. Outer pane remains intact.','Cabin air → gap'),('Normal load',at('pressure','normally'),S('backup'),'Airflow recedes; a distinct amber pressure-load graphic identifies the outer pane.','Normal load → outer'),('Backup condition',S('backup'),at('backup','scratch'),'Explicit hypothetical: the outer pane becomes a ghost outline, then the pressure-load annotation moves to the inner pane.','If the outer pane fails'),('Return to cabin',at('backup','scratch'),dur,'The same three panes recombine, returning to the passenger view. Protector role and final three-layer takeaway.','Three layers. Different jobs.')]
    return [(name,a,b,obj,'Model x 240–840, y 650–1110; leaders above.','Pale cabin daylight','Absolute-time camera orbit and smooth separation.','Word anchors with cubic easing.','Perspective camera, slow continuous movement.',COLOUR_LANGUAGE,labels,'Soft fade / same model continuation','Quiet original filtered-air ambience; no effects.',name) for name,a,b,obj,labels in items]
